leds: lgm-sso: keep DUTY_CYCLE at full in non-HS modes

Vendor stock firmware sets DUTY_CYCLE to 0xff for every active LED
output and never changes it after init; on/off is driven entirely by
SSO_CPU bit toggles. Mainline lgm-sso instead writes
DUTY_CYCLE(pin) = brightness in sso_led_brightness_set() — and seeds
DUTY_CYCLE(pin) = brightness (= 0) in sso_led_hw_cfg(). With duty
cycle at 0 the SSO output is held at idle level regardless of the
SSO_CPU bit, so subsequent bit toggles never reach the external shift
register and the LED state never changes. SW/FPID modes don't use
PWM dimming, so this duty-cycle-from-brightness path is wrong on
real boards regardless.

Seed DUTY_CYCLE to LED_FULL on LED creation and stop touching it from
brightness_set(). PWM dimming via DUTY_CYCLE only applies in GPTC-HS
mode and the corresponding write can be added back behind that gate
when HS support is hooked up.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -242,7 +242,6 @@ static void sso_led_brightness_set(struc
 	desc = &led->desc;
 
 	desc->brightness = brightness;
-	regmap_write(priv->mmap, DUTY_CYCLE(desc->pin), brightness);
 
 	if (brightness == LED_OFF)
 		val = 0;
@@ -337,10 +336,8 @@ static void sso_led_hw_cfg(struct sso_le
 		regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, SSO_CON3, BIT(desc->pin),
 				   1 << desc->pin);
 
-	/* set brightness */
-	regmap_write(priv->mmap, DUTY_CYCLE(desc->pin), desc->brightness);
+	regmap_write(priv->mmap, DUTY_CYCLE(desc->pin), LED_FULL);
 
-	/* enable output */
 	if (!desc->hw_trig && desc->brightness)
 		gpiod_set_value(led->gpiod, 1);
 }
